{"strongs": "H6666", "word": "צְדָקָה", "translit": "tse.da.qah", "root": "צדק", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "righteousness", "definition": "צְדָקָה 157 noun feminine righteousness ; — absolute ׳ צ Gen 15:6 +81 t.; construct צִדְקַת Deut 33:21 +5 t.; suffix צִדְקָתִי Gen 30:33 +, etc.; plural צְדָקוֺת Isa 33:15 +3 t.; construct צִדְקוֺת Judg 5:11 +; suffix צִדְקֹתֶיךָ Dan 9:16 , etc.; — 1. righteousness , in government: \\ \\ a. of judge, ruler, king: || משׁפט Isa 5:7 ; Isa 9:6 ; Amos 5:7 ; Amos 6:12 ׳ משׁפט וצ 2Sam 8:15 , עשׂה David executed justice and righteousness = 1Chr 18:14 , compare 1Kgs 10:9 = 2Chr 9:8 ; Jer 22:3 ; Jer 22:15 ; Jer 33:15 ; Ezek 45:9 יִכּוֺן כִּסֵּא ׳ בּצ Prov 16:12 , compare Isa 54:14 ׳ עֲבֹדַת השׂ , ׳ מַעֲשֵׂה הצ Isa 32:17 , compare V:16; ׳ נֹגְשַׂיִךְ צ Isa 60:17 . \\ \\ b. of law, || משׁפטים , ׳ צִדְקַת י Deut 33:21 . \\ \\ c. of Davidic king, Messiah, || משׁפט , Ps 72:1 ; Ps 72:3 ; Isa 9:6 ; Jer 23:5 ; Jer 33:15 . 2. God's attribute as sovereign Ps 36:7 ; Ps 71:19 in government, עשׂה ׳ משׁפט וצ Ps 99:4 ; Jer 9:23 administering justice Job 37:28 punishment Isa 1:27 ; Isa 5:16 ; Isa 10:22 ; Isa 28:17 ; Dan 9:7 vindication of his people Mic 7:9 . 3. righteousness , in a case or cause, בצדקתי החזקתי Job 27:6 on my righteousness I hold fast ; ׳ מה ישׁ לי עוד צ 2Sam 19:29 what right have I yet ? of God's judgments, ׳ הגיד צ Isa 57:12 (iron.); ׳ השׁיב צ 1Sam 26:23 ; Job 33:26 ׳ כּצ , השׁיב 2Sam 22:25 , גמל v 2Sam 22:21 , נתן 1Kgs 8:52 = 2Chr 6:23 . 4. righteousness = truthfulness , ׳ באמת ובצ Isa 48:1 ; Zech 8:8 in word Isa 45:28 ; Isa 63:1 , oath Jer 4:2 . 5. righteousness , as ethically right: Gen 30:33 ( J ) Deut 6:25 ; Isa 33:5 ; Isa 41:18 ; Ezek 14:14 ; Ezek 14:20 ; Prov 10:2 ; Prov 11:4 ; Prov 11:5 ; Prov 11:18 ; Prov 11:19 +17 t., + צִדְקַת (ה)צַדִּיק(יםׅ Isa 5:23 ; Ezek 18:20 ; Ezek 33:12 ישׁרים ׳ צ Prov 11:6 ׳ אֹרַח צ Prov 8:20 ; Prov 12:28 ׳ דֶּרֶךְ צ Prov 16:31 ׳ עשׂה צ do righteousness Ps 106:3 ; Isa 56:1 ; Isa 58:2 ; Ezek 18:22 ׳ עשׂה משׁפט וצ Ezek 18:5 +6 t. Ezekiel; ומשׁפט ׳ עשׂה צ Gen 18:10 ( J ) Prov 21:8 ׳ רדף צ Prov 15:9 ; Prov 21:21 ׳ הלך באמת ובצ 1 k Prov 3:6 ׳ חשׁב לוֺ (ל)צ Gen 15:6 ( J E ) imputed to him ( for ) righteousness , Ps 106:31 וָחֶסֶד ׳ צ Prov 21:21 (twice in verse) (strike out ᵐ5 A B Toy). 6. righteousness as vindicated, justification, salvation , etc. (compare צֶדֶק 6 ): \\ \\ a. of God || יָשַׁע , תְּשׁוּעָה , יְשׁוּעָה Isa 45:8 ; Isa 46:13 ; Isa 51:6 +7 t. Isa 2 ; || בְּרָכָה Ps 24:6 || נַחֲלָה Isa 54:17 || חֶסֶד Ps 36:11 ; Ps 103:17 ׳ שֶׁמֶשׁ צ Mal 3:20 sun of righteousness (with healing); ׳ בִּצ , ׳ י delivers, guides, exalts his people Ps 5:9 ; Ps 31:2 ; Ps 71:2 ; Ps 89:17 ; Ps 119:40 ; Ps 143:1 ; Ps 143:11 אַליָֿבאֹוּ בְּצִדְקָתֶ֑ךָ Ps 69:28 (of wicked); as accusative after verbs of declaring, etc., his saving ( delivering ) righteousness Ps 22:32 ; Ps 40:11 ; Ps 51:16 ; Ps 71:15 ; Ps 71:16 ; Ps 71:24 ; Ps 98:2 ; Ps 145:7 also ׳ יִוָּדַע צ Ps 88:13 עֹמֶדֶת ׳ צ לָעַד his righteousness endureth for ever Ps 111:3 compare Ps 119:142 . \\ \\ b. of people, = prosperity , || הון , עשׁר Prov 8:18 ׳ מוֺרֶה לצ early rain for prosperity Joel 2:23 . 7. plural righteous acts: \\ \\ a. of God Judg 5:11 (twice in verse); 1Sam 12:7 ; Mic 6:5 vindication of right Ps 103:6 redemptive Isa 45:24 ; Dan 9:16 . \\ \\ b. of man's moral conduct Isa 64:5 ; Jer 51:10 , also probably Ezek 3:20 ; Ezek 18:24 ; Ezek 33:13 ( Kt singular) Ps 11:7 (? gloss), Dan 9:18 as adverb accusative, הֹלֵךְ צְדָקוֺת Isa 33:15 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6942')\">BDB6942</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6666')\">H6666</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6941')\">BDB6941</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6943')\">BDB6943</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>צְדָקָה</bdbheb><sub>157</sub> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>righteousness</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>צ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 15:6\" b=\